{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"The entry-kind read corrects the framing of the StopSign-resync account and sharpens the defect. Nodes 3 and 4 hold identical kinds at indices 35, 36 and 37: a decided value, the StopSign, and nothing. Their logs therefore agree at the reconfiguration position, and leader 4 did not lose the StopSign entry. What differs is the cached state and the decided index: node 4 reports is_reconfigured None even though its log holds a StopSign at index 36, and it reports decided 38 while its accepted index is 37 and its log ends at index 36, so its decided index exceeds its own log. Node 3, whose cached StopSign is still present, reports accepted 37 and decided 37. The update records these facts as a new knowledge entry, revises the question's hypothesis from a leader whose log lacks the marker to a cleared cache plus a decided index beyond the local log, and restates the interpretation: sync_log's clearing branch removes the cached marker without removing the appended entry, handle_accepted sets the leader's decided index from follower-reported accepted indices without comparing it to the leader's own accepted index, and node 3's sequence-expected Decides clamp decided at 37 with no reconnect while resends reuse consumed sequence numbers. The interpretation also states explicitly that the zero divergence count is a limitation of the decided-values comparison, which ignores StopSign entries and prefix length, rather than evidence of agreement. No execution is requested.\"}"}}
